   'Which method is used to evaluate the financial feasibility of a forestry project by calculating the present value of expected future cash flows and comparing it to the initial investment cost?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Internal Rate of Return (IRR)"},{"id":"b","text":"Net Present Value (NPV)"},{"id":"c","text":"Payback Period"},{"id":"d","text":"Return on Investment (ROI)"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00123', 'forest-production', 'forest-economics-finance', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In forest finance, what is the significance of using Weighted Average Cost of Capital (WACC) when evaluating forestry projects?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It is used to calculate the future value of cash flows."},{"id":"b","text":"It measures the liquidity of a forestry project."},{"id":"c","text":"It is used to determine the real rate of return on investment."},{"id":"d","text":"It represents the average rate of return required by all of the company''s investors."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00124', 'forest-production', 'forest-economics-finance', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'A forest manager is assessing a reforestation project expected to generate varying annual cash flows over a period of 10 years. Which financial metric would be most appropriate to evaluate the project''s viability?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Simple Payback Period"},{"id":"b","text":"Internal Rate of Return (IRR)"},{"id":"c","text":"Profitability Index"},{"id":"d","text":"Net Present Value (NPV)"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00125', 'forest-production', 'forest-economics-finance', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What does the term ''hurdle rate'' refer to in the context of forest project investment appraisal?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"The rate of return below which a project is automatically accepted."},{"id":"b","text":"The minimum acceptable rate of return required by investors."},{"id":"c","text":"The average rate of return of all projects in the industry."},{"id":"d","text":"The maximum rate of return a project can achieve."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00126', 'forest-production', 'forest-economics-finance', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'When evaluating forest investments, what role does sensitivity analysis play in assessing project risk?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It identifies how changing one variable affects the project''s NPV."},{"id":"b","text":"It determines the payback period of the project."},{"id":"c","text":"It calculates the exact cost of capital for the project."},{"id":"d","text":"It measures the liquidity of a forestry project."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00127', 'forest-production', 'forest-economics-finance', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In evaluating a forestry project''s financial performance, which of the following analyses would you use to assess how a project''s NPV responds to changes in key assumptions such as timber price and discount rate?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Break-even analysis"},{"id":"b","text":"Scenario analysis"},{"id":"c","text":"Sensitivity analysis"},{"id":"d","text":"Cost-benefit analysis"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00128', 'forest-production', 'forest-economics-finance', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which of the following best describes the purpose of conducting a break-even analysis in forest project management?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To determine the point at which revenue equals fixed and variable costs."},{"id":"b","text":"To calculate the future value of cash flows."},{"id":"c","text":"To evaluate the project''s environmental impact."},{"id":"d","text":"To determine the project''s liquidity ratio."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00129', 'forest-production', 'forest-economics-finance', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In forest economics, what is the implication of a forestry project having a Profitability Index (PI) greater than 1?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"The project is expected to break even."},{"id":"b","text":"The project is considered financially viable."},{"id":"c","text":"The project has a net loss."},{"id":"d","text":"The project does not cover its capital costs."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00130', 'forest-production', 'forest-economics-finance', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'When appraising a forestry investment, why is it important to consider the time value of money?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It allows for the comparison of cash flows occurring at different times."},{"id":"b","text":"It ensures that all project costs are accounted for in current monetary terms."},{"id":"c","text":"It adjusts future revenues for inflation only."},{"id":"d","text":"It indicates the future value of a project without considering its present cost."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00131', 'forest-production', 'forest-economics-finance', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'A forestry company is considering two potential projects: Project X and Project Y. Project X requires an initial investment of PHP 5 million and is expected to generate annual cash inflows of PHP 1 million for 7 years. Project Y requires an initial investment of PHP 3 million and is expected to generate annual cash inflows of PHP 700,000 for 5 years. If the company''s required rate of return is 10%, which project has a higher Net Present Value (NPV)?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Project X has a higher NPV."},{"id":"b","text":"Project Y has a higher NPV."},{"id":"c","text":"Both projects have the same NPV."},{"id":"d","text":"Neither project has a positive NPV."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00132', 'forest-production', 'forest-economics-finance', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of forest economics, a company is trying to decide whether to invest in a plantation project that involves the cost of land acquisition at PHP 2 million and planting costs of PHP 500,000. Expected annual revenues from the plantation are PHP 300,000, and the project life is 20 years. If the company''s discount rate is 8%, what is the project''s Benefit-Cost Ratio (BCR) and is it financially viable?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"BCR is 0.85 and the project is not financially viable."},{"id":"b","text":"BCR is 1.02 and the project is financially viable."},{"id":"c","text":"BCR is 1.15 and the project is financially viable."},{"id":"d","text":"BCR is 0.78 and the project is not financially viable."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00133', 'forest-production', 'forest-economics-finance', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'A forestry company is evaluating an investment in a teak plantation. The project requires an initial investment of PHP 8 million and is expected to generate annual cash inflows of PHP 1.5 million for 15 years. If the company''s required rate of return is 12%, what is the Net Present Value (NPV) of the project? Use the formula NPV = Σ (Cash inflow / (1 + r)^n) - Initial investment, where r is the discount rate and n is the year.',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"PHP 3,809,000"},{"id":"b","text":"PHP 2,034,000"},{"id":"c","text":"PHP 1,456,000"},{"id":"d","text":"PHP 2,678,000"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00134', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the primary goal of range management in the context of forestry?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To maximize livestock production at all costs."},{"id":"b","text":"To eliminate all native vegetation."},{"id":"c","text":"To balance the needs of livestock, wildlife, and natural resources."},{"id":"d","text":"To convert forest land into agricultural land."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00135', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which of the following is a common method used in range management to improve forage quality?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Overgrazing the area."},{"id":"b","text":"Deforestation."},{"id":"c","text":"Prescribed burning."},{"id":"d","text":"Urbanization."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00136', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which Philippine law ensures the protection of indigenous peoples'' rights, which can include access to rangelands?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"PD 705"},{"id":"b","text":"RA 7586"},{"id":"c","text":"RA 9147"},{"id":"d","text":"RA 8371"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00137', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the term for the sustainable use of natural forages by livestock in a specific area?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Overgrazing"},{"id":"b","text":"Rotational grazing"},{"id":"c","text":"Selective breeding"},{"id":"d","text":"Terracing"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00138', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which of the following is a key component of a range management plan?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Crop rotation schedule"},{"id":"b","text":"Aquatic species inventory"},{"id":"c","text":"Timber extraction plan"},{"id":"d","text":"Grazing capacity assessment"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
