   'Which of the following practices ensures that plant species diversity is maintained in rangelands?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Continuous grazing"},{"id":"b","text":"Prescribed grazing"},{"id":"c","text":"Selective logging"},{"id":"d","text":"Urban sprawl"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00140', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the term for the maximum number of animals a range area can support without causing degradation?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Carrying capacity"},{"id":"b","text":"Stocking rate"},{"id":"c","text":"Overgrazing threshold"},{"id":"d","text":"Grazing intensity"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00141', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which agency in the Philippines is primarily responsible for managing public rangelands?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Department of Environment and Natural Resources (DENR)"},{"id":"b","text":"Department of Agriculture"},{"id":"c","text":"Bureau of Fisheries and Aquatic Resources"},{"id":"d","text":"Department of Public Works and Highways"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00142', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is rotational grazing primarily designed to achieve?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Increase soil erosion rates."},{"id":"b","text":"Clear land for agriculture."},{"id":"c","text":"Eliminate all predators."},{"id":"d","text":"Allow recovery of forage plants."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00143', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which Philippine regulation outlines the conservation of terrestrial and marine areas, including rangelands, within the National Integrated Protected Areas System?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"PD 705"},{"id":"b","text":"RA 8371"},{"id":"c","text":"RA 11038"},{"id":"d","text":"RA 9147"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00144', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the primary purpose of implementing a carrying capacity in range management?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To maximize the number of livestock regardless of rangeland condition."},{"id":"b","text":"To prevent overgrazing and ensure sustainability of the rangeland."},{"id":"c","text":"To exclusively promote the growth of certain plant species."},{"id":"d","text":"To increase the economic value of livestock products."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00145', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which type of grazing system involves dividing rangeland into multiple paddocks and rotating livestock between them?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Continuous grazing"},{"id":"b","text":"Deferred grazing"},{"id":"c","text":"Rotational grazing"},{"id":"d","text":"Strip grazing"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00146', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the term for a plant community''s ability to recover after being grazed?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Restoration potential"},{"id":"b","text":"Resilience"},{"id":"c","text":"Regeneration capacity"},{"id":"d","text":"Reclamation ability"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00147', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which of the following is a primary concern in range management regarding soil?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Soil acidity"},{"id":"b","text":"Soil salinity"},{"id":"c","text":"Soil compaction"},{"id":"d","text":"Soil erosion"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00148', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'In the context of range management, what does ''stocking rate'' refer to?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"The speed at which livestock gain weight"},{"id":"b","text":"The number of livestock per unit area of rangeland"},{"id":"c","text":"The total number of livestock on the farm"},{"id":"d","text":"The rate of livestock reproduction"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00149', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Easy', 'practice',
