  ('fp-g00176', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which indigenous plant species is often considered in Philippine range management for its resilience and nutritional value?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Narra / Pterocarpus indicus / Fabaceae"},{"id":"b","text":"Bamboo / Bambusa blumeana / Poaceae"},{"id":"c","text":"Cogon grass / Imperata cylindrica / Poaceae"},{"id":"d","text":"Banana / Musa acuminata / Musaceae"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00177', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'How can the implementation of controlled burning benefit rangelands in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Increases soil acidity"},{"id":"b","text":"Encourages invasive species growth"},{"id":"c","text":"Reduces pest populations"},{"id":"d","text":"Promotes soil erosion"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00178', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'What is the recommended practice to ensure the sustainability of forage plants in heavily grazed areas?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Rest periods"},{"id":"b","text":"Continuous grazing"},{"id":"c","text":"Seed harvesting"},{"id":"d","text":"Herbicide application"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00179', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which of the following strategies is most effective in managing the risk of overgrazing on rangelands?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Increasing livestock numbers"},{"id":"b","text":"Implementing rotational grazing"},{"id":"c","text":"Developing new water sources"},{"id":"d","text":"Deploying electric fences"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00180', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which practice in range management is primarily used to control encroachment of woody plants into grassland areas?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Grazing exclusion"},{"id":"b","text":"Herbivore introduction"},{"id":"c","text":"Mechanical clearing"},{"id":"d","text":"Intensive cropping"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00181', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of range management, what is a key distinction between continuous grazing and rotational grazing systems in terms of plant recovery and soil impact?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Continuous grazing allows for better plant recovery and less soil compaction."},{"id":"b","text":"Continuous grazing requires less management but leads to better soil health."},{"id":"c","text":"Rotational grazing generally prevents overgrazing and improves soil health more effectively."},{"id":"d","text":"Rotational grazing results in more uniform forage use but increases soil erosion."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00182', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which of the following factors most significantly affects the carrying capacity of a rangeland in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Animal breed and size"},{"id":"b","text":"Seasonal rainfall variability"},{"id":"c","text":"Type of grazing system implemented"},{"id":"d","text":"Distance from water sources"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00183', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'How is the concept of ''rest period'' in rotational grazing systems crucial for maintaining long-term productivity of rangelands, especially in the Philippine context?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It increases the immediate forage yield by 50%."},{"id":"b","text":"It provides sufficient recovery time for plant regrowth and soil nutrients replenishment."},{"id":"c","text":"It allows the soil structure to remain compacted, preventing erosion."},{"id":"d","text":"It eliminates the need for periodic fertilization."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00184', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In a range management scenario, if a rangeland is divided into 5 paddocks with equal area, and each paddock is grazed for 6 days followed by a rest period of 24 days, what is the total cycle duration before returning to the first paddock?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"50 days"},{"id":"b","text":"75 days"},{"id":"c","text":"30 days"},{"id":"d","text":"60 days"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00185', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is the primary advantage of using mixed-species grazing in Philippine rangeland management?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Enhances biodiversity and improves forage utilization."},{"id":"b","text":"Increases the risk of disease transmission among livestock."},{"id":"c","text":"Simplifies management by concentrating on a single forage species."},{"id":"d","text":"Reduces soil fertility over time."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00186', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the management of rangelands, why is it important to monitor the phenological stages of dominant forage species?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To determine the economic value of the rangeland."},{"id":"b","text":"To align grazing periods with peak nutritional value and recovery potential."},{"id":"c","text":"To prevent the establishment of invasive plant species."},{"id":"d","text":"To ensure uniform soil moisture levels across the rangeland."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00187', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which of the following practices is used to evaluate the condition and trend of a rangeland ecosystem in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Frequent plowing of the soil surface."},{"id":"b","text":"Regular rangeland health assessment surveys."},{"id":"c","text":"Seasonal livestock migration."},{"id":"d","text":"Constant application of chemical fertilizers."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00188', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of range management in the Philippines, what is the critical goal of implementing a stocking rate that matches the carrying capacity of the land?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To maximize short-term economic return."},{"id":"b","text":"To increase the frequency of rotational grazing."},{"id":"c","text":"To promote rapid plant growth through overstocking."},{"id":"d","text":"To ensure the sustainability of the forage resource."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00189', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'When implementing a grazing system in a Philippine context, what is a significant benefit of incorporating indigenous forage species over exotic ones?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Higher resistance to local pests and diseases."},{"id":"b","text":"Increased water demand and higher management costs."},{"id":"c","text":"Rapid spread and dominance over native species."},{"id":"d","text":"Reduced adaptability to local climatic conditions."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00190', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of range management, which ecological process is primarily enhanced by implementing a rotational grazing system in Philippine rangelands?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Increased soil erosion"},{"id":"b","text":"Decreased plant biodiversity"},{"id":"c","text":"Improved nutrient cycling"},{"id":"d","text":"Higher water runoff"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00191', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which of the following scenarios would most likely require a reevaluation of the stocking rate on a Philippine rangeland?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Introduction of new exotic plant species that are less palatable to livestock."},{"id":"b","text":"Expansion of local wildlife populations that utilize the same forage resources as livestock."},{"id":"c","text":"An unusually wet season causing a temporary increase in forage production."},{"id":"d","text":"Installation of new fencing to improve paddock rotation efficiency."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00192', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which of the following strategies would best address the challenge of maintaining forage quality in a rangeland predominantly covered with Imperata cylindrica (Cogon grass) in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Frequent burning of the grassland to promote new growth."},{"id":"b","text":"Introducing a diverse mix of legumes to improve soil nitrogen levels."},{"id":"c","text":"Increasing the stocking rate to control grass height."},{"id":"d","text":"Applying chemical fertilizers to boost grass production."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00193', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'A range manager plans to establish a controlled rotational grazing system on a 100-hectare rangeland. If the desired stocking rate is 1.5 Animal Units (AU) per hectare, what is the total number of Animal Units that should be allocated to this rangeland?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"75 AU"},{"id":"b","text":"100 AU"},{"id":"c","text":"200 AU"},{"id":"d","text":"150 AU"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00194', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In a rangeland with significant topographical variation in the Philippines, which management practice is crucial for preventing soil erosion while maintaining optimal grazing pressure?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Establishing contour buffer strips along slopes."},{"id":"b","text":"Using fixed stocking rates throughout the year."},{"id":"c","text":"Implementing continuous grazing."},{"id":"d","text":"Relying on natural water sources for livestock distribution."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00195', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is a potential consequence of overstocking in a rangeland ecosystem characterized by low forage productivity during the dry season in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Degradation of the soil and reduction in forage quality."},{"id":"b","text":"Increased forage availability in the following wet season."},{"id":"c","text":"Enhanced resilience of the rangeland ecosystem."},{"id":"d","text":"Stabilized plant and animal biodiversity."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00196', 'forest-production', 'range-management', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of range management, a manager wants to determine the appropriate stocking rate for a 50-hectare rangeland predominantly covered with Andropogon gayanus. The carrying capacity of Andropogon gayanus is known to be 0.8 Animal Units (AU) per hectare per year. However, due to seasonal variations, the effective forage availability is reduced by 15%. What is the adjusted total stocking rate for the rangeland?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"40 AU"},{"id":"b","text":"50 AU"},{"id":"c","text":"34 AU"},{"id":"d","text":"42.5 AU"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00197', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which of the following is a primary objective of multiple uses forestry?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Maximize timber production only"},{"id":"b","text":"Conserve biodiversity only"},{"id":"c","text":"Ensure sustainable use of forest resources for various purposes"},{"id":"d","text":"Focus exclusively on recreation and tourism"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
