  ('fp-g00216', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which of the following is a critical aspect of implementing multiple uses forestry in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Protecting commercial interest only"},{"id":"b","text":"Balancing ecological, economic, and social values"},{"id":"c","text":"Focusing solely on timber production"},{"id":"d","text":"Eliminating human access to forests"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00217', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In multiple uses forestry, which ecosystem service is most directly enhanced by maintaining watershed integrity?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Carbon sequestration"},{"id":"b","text":"Water regulation"},{"id":"c","text":"Recreation opportunities"},{"id":"d","text":"Biodiversity conservation"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00218', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which of the following practices is crucial for achieving the goals of multiple uses forestry?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Monoculture planting"},{"id":"b","text":"Clear-cutting techniques"},{"id":"c","text":"Integrated land management"},{"id":"d","text":"Exclusive wildlife conservation"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00219', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'How does multiple uses forestry benefit indigenous communities in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By restricting their access to forest resources"},{"id":"b","text":"By enforcing relocation programs"},{"id":"c","text":"By integrating traditional knowledge in forest management"},{"id":"d","text":"By prioritizing tourism over forest conservation"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00220', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In multiple uses forestry, what role do non-timber forest products (NTFPs) play?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"They are considered wastage and removed during management."},{"id":"b","text":"They are the sole focus of conservation efforts."},{"id":"c","text":"They provide additional income and support biodiversity."},{"id":"d","text":"They are irrelevant to forest management goals."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00221', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which strategy in multiple uses forestry involves zoning different forest areas for specific uses to prevent conflicts?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Rotational grazing"},{"id":"b","text":"Selective logging"},{"id":"c","text":"Land-use planning"},{"id":"d","text":"Fire suppression"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00222', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In multiple uses forestry, which factor is essential for monitoring and assessing forest health over time?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Timber revenue tracking"},{"id":"b","text":"Biodiversity inventory"},{"id":"c","text":"Tourism statistics"},{"id":"d","text":"Infrastructure development"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00223', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which of the following represents a consumptive use of forests in the context of multiple uses forestry?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Bird watching"},{"id":"b","text":"Hiking"},{"id":"c","text":"Timber harvesting"},{"id":"d","text":"Photography"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00224', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In the practice of multiple uses forestry, why is community involvement considered vital?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It ensures higher profit margins for logging companies."},{"id":"b","text":"It leads to more sustainable and accepted management practices."},{"id":"c","text":"It minimizes the importance of ecological values."},{"id":"d","text":"It focuses management solely on recreational uses."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00225', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which type of forest use is prioritized under the multiple uses forestry approach to ensure sustainability?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Short-term economic gains through intensive logging"},{"id":"b","text":"Exclusive wildlife conservation without human interaction"},{"id":"c","text":"Long-term balanced use considering ecological, economic, and social factors"},{"id":"d","text":"Recreational use as the only acceptable activity"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00226', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which of the following best describes the concept of ''carrying capacity'' in the context of multiple uses forestry?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"The total amount of timber that can be harvested annually from a forest."},{"id":"b","text":"The maximum number of visitors a forest area can sustain without environmental degradation."},{"id":"c","text":"The diversity of plant species that can be supported within a forest ecosystem."},{"id":"d","text":"The ability of a forest to regenerate after a natural disturbance."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00227', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In multiple uses forestry, which of the following practices helps in minimizing conflicts between timber production and wildlife conservation?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Intensive monoculture plantations."},{"id":"b","text":"Clear-cutting large areas of forest."},{"id":"c","text":"Exclusive focus on maximizing timber yield."},{"id":"d","text":"Implementing buffer zones around sensitive habitats."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00228', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which forest management practice is often used in multiple uses forestry to maintain biodiversity while allowing timber extraction?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Selective logging."},{"id":"b","text":"Complete deforestation."},{"id":"c","text":"Slash-and-burn agriculture."},{"id":"d","text":"Replanting with exotic species."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00229', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In the context of multiple uses forestry, what is the primary benefit of integrating agroforestry systems?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Enhances biodiversity and provides additional income sources."},{"id":"b","text":"Increases soil erosion."},{"id":"c","text":"Reduces water availability for crops."},{"id":"d","text":"Limits the growth of native forest species."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00230', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which of the following is a key principle of multiple uses forestry when balancing timber production and watershed protection?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Prioritizing timber production over all other uses."},{"id":"b","text":"Converting forest land to agricultural use."},{"id":"c","text":"Implementing sustainable harvesting techniques."},{"id":"d","text":"Eliminating all recreational activities within forest areas."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00231', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'How does multiple uses forestry address the challenge of fire management in forest areas?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By using controlled burns to reduce fuel loads and prevent large wildfires."},{"id":"b","text":"By suppressing all fires to protect forest resources."},{"id":"c","text":"By allowing wildfires to burn unchecked for ecological benefits."},{"id":"d","text":"By planting fire-resistant exotic species exclusively."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00232', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In multiple uses forestry, what is the role of forest certification schemes?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To promote illegal logging practices."},{"id":"b","text":"To ensure all harvested timber is from uncertified sources."},{"id":"c","text":"To verify sustainable forest management practices and promote market access."},{"id":"d","text":"To restrict the sale of all forest products."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00233', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'What is an essential factor to consider in multiple uses forestry to ensure the sustainable provision of ecosystem services?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Maximizing short-term economic gains."},{"id":"b","text":"Maintaining forest cover and ecological integrity."},{"id":"c","text":"Ignoring environmental regulations."},{"id":"d","text":"Focusing solely on timber extraction."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00234', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'What strategy is often employed in multiple uses forestry to reconcile the interests of various stakeholders?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Implementing strict top-down management policies."},{"id":"b","text":"Prioritizing only commercial logging interests."},{"id":"c","text":"Excluding community involvement from forest planning."},{"id":"d","text":"Facilitating participatory forest management and decision-making processes."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00235', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In multiple uses forestry, which method helps ensure the sustainable harvest of non-timber forest products?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Overharvesting to maximize profit."},{"id":"b","text":"Implementing a rotational harvesting system."},{"id":"c","text":"Harvesting all available resources at once."},{"id":"d","text":"Ignoring the local community''s traditional practices and knowledge."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00236', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In multiple uses forestry, what is the purpose of establishing buffer zones around protected areas?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To provide additional habitat for wildlife and reduce human-wildlife conflicts"},{"id":"b","text":"To maximize timber production in adjacent areas"},{"id":"c","text":"To limit the recreational use of forests"},{"id":"d","text":"To increase agricultural outputs by utilizing forest margins"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00237', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which approach in multiple uses forestry aims to enhance soil fertility and prevent erosion while allowing for timber production?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Clear-cut logging"},{"id":"b","text":"Monoculture plantations"},{"id":"c","text":"Agroforestry systems"},{"id":"d","text":"Selective logging"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00238', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In terms of forest production management, why is it important to incorporate non-timber forest products (NTFPs) into multiple uses forestry plans?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"NTFPs support local economies and biodiversity while providing sustainable income."},{"id":"b","text":"NTFPs provide a quick return on investment compared to timber products."},{"id":"c","text":"NTFPs are easier to harvest than timber."},{"id":"d","text":"NTFPs require less management than timber resources, thus reducing costs."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00239', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'How does the implementation of multiple uses forestry contribute to climate change mitigation?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"By increasing the rate of deforestation in designated areas"},{"id":"b","text":"By promoting the rapid growth of monoculture plantations"},{"id":"c","text":"By focusing exclusively on fuelwood production"},{"id":"d","text":"By maintaining forest carbon stocks and enhancing carbon sequestration"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00240', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'What role does community-based forest management play in multiple uses forestry?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It centralizes decision-making to improve efficiency."},{"id":"b","text":"It removes local communities from forest areas to prevent overuse."},{"id":"c","text":"It focuses solely on the commercial use of forests."},{"id":"d","text":"It empowers local communities to participate in sustainable forest management."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00241', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In a multiple uses forestry framework, why is zoning an effective management tool?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It restricts all forms of forest use to conservation purposes."},{"id":"b","text":"It allows for the exclusive use of forests for recreational activities."},{"id":"c","text":"It separates different forest uses to minimize user conflicts and optimize resource benefits."},{"id":"d","text":"It eliminates the need for management plans by assigning uses to all forest areas."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00242', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In the context of multiple uses forestry in the Philippines, which tree species is often utilized for both timber production and its medicinal properties?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Narra / Pterocarpus indicus / Fabaceae"},{"id":"b","text":"Banaba / Lagerstroemia speciosa / Lythraceae"},{"id":"c","text":"Ilang-ilang / Cananga odorata / Annonaceae"},{"id":"d","text":"Mahogany / Swietenia macrophylla / Meliaceae"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00243', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of multiple uses forestry, how is the concept of ''adaptive management'' applied to balance economic, ecological, and social objectives?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Regularly revising management strategies based on monitoring and new data."},{"id":"b","text":"Implementing a fixed management plan regardless of changing conditions."},{"id":"c","text":"Focusing exclusively on maximizing timber yields without regard to other uses."},{"id":"d","text":"Establishing permanent zoning that does not account for stakeholder feedback."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00244', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'When considering the trade-offs in multiple uses forestry, which approach would best address the issue of biodiversity conservation while allowing sustainable timber extraction?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Clear-cutting large areas to maximize timber yield."},{"id":"b","text":"Focusing solely on monoculture plantations for timber."},{"id":"c","text":"Prioritizing recreation over all other forest uses."},{"id":"d","text":"Implementing selective logging with biodiversity corridors."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00245', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In multiple uses forestry, how can the principle of ''ecosystem services'' be integrated into forest management plans to optimize both timber and non-timber benefits?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Ignoring non-timber benefits to enhance timber production."},{"id":"b","text":"Incorporating valuation of all ecosystem services in decision-making."},{"id":"c","text":"Valuing only the direct economic returns from timber sales."},{"id":"d","text":"Excluding water and soil conservation from management plans."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00246', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is a key challenge when integrating ecotourism into multiple uses forestry in a way that supports biodiversity conservation?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Maximizing tourism revenue without ecological considerations."},{"id":"b","text":"Developing extensive infrastructure in sensitive areas."},{"id":"c","text":"Promoting unrestricted access to all forest areas."},{"id":"d","text":"Limiting visitor numbers to reduce environmental impact."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00247', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which strategy in multiple uses forestry is designed to ensure that non-timber forest products (NTFPs) are harvested sustainably while maintaining forest health?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Rotational clear-cutting of NTFP areas."},{"id":"b","text":"Adopting a blanket ban on NTFP collection."},{"id":"c","text":"Allowing unrestricted access to NTFPs year-round."},{"id":"d","text":"Implementing community-based monitoring and quotas."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00248', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the practice of multiple uses forestry, how can conflicting interests between timber production and watershed protection be reconciled?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Implementing integrated watershed management practices."},{"id":"b","text":"Prioritizing timber production over all other uses."},{"id":"c","text":"Focusing solely on the economic value of timber."},{"id":"d","text":"Ignoring the importance of watersheds in forest management."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00249', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'How does the concept of ''ecosystem-based management'' apply to multiple uses forestry in the context of maintaining forest resilience?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Focusing only on maximizing economic output from timber."},{"id":"b","text":"Incorporating ecological processes and functions in management decisions."},{"id":"c","text":"Ignoring ecological functions to streamline management."},{"id":"d","text":"Minimizing stakeholder involvement in management plans."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00250', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What role does stakeholder participation play in the successful implementation of multiple uses forestry in community-managed forests?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Involving stakeholders to incorporate diverse perspectives and knowledge."},{"id":"b","text":"Excluding local communities to ensure top-down decision-making."},{"id":"c","text":"Ignoring the needs and knowledge of indigenous peoples."},{"id":"d","text":"Focusing exclusively on government mandates without local input."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00251', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of multiple uses forestry, what is the importance of having an adaptive management plan for fire control and prevention?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To establish a one-time fire control strategy that doesn''t need updates."},{"id":"b","text":"To allow for dynamic responses to changing fire regimes and conditions."},{"id":"c","text":"To focus only on post-fire rehabilitation efforts."},{"id":"d","text":"To solely rely on traditional fire fighting methods without innovation."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00252', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In multiple uses forestry, why is it critical to align forest management practices with the principles of climate change adaptation?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To enhance the resilience of forest ecosystems to changing climate conditions."},{"id":"b","text":"To ensure forests are managed exclusively for carbon sequestration."},{"id":"c","text":"To ignore climate impacts and focus solely on immediate economic gains."},{"id":"d","text":"To promote deforestation for short-term agricultural expansion."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00253', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In multiple uses forestry, a key challenge is balancing timber production with the conservation of biodiversity. Which management practice helps achieve this balance by allowing selective logging while maintaining ecological integrity?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Clearcutting with buffer zones"},{"id":"b","text":"Shelterwood cutting"},{"id":"c","text":"Selective logging with retention of key habitat structures"},{"id":"d","text":"Entire area logging rotation"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00254', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of the Philippines, multiple uses forestry includes the utilization of bamboo, which is both an economic and ecological resource. Which genus of bamboo, commonly used for furniture and construction, is native to the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Fargesia"},{"id":"b","text":"Phyllostachys"},{"id":"c","text":"Dendrocalamus"},{"id":"d","text":"Bambusa"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00255', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In multiple uses forestry, integrating agroforestry systems can enhance both productivity and ecological balance. Which of the following practices combines tree planting with crops or livestock to improve land use efficiency?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Silvicultural grazing"},{"id":"b","text":"Clearcutting"},{"id":"c","text":"Alley cropping"},{"id":"d","text":"High-density monoculture"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00256', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which of the following represents the integration of ecosystem services into a multiple uses forestry plan aimed at optimizing both timber and non-timber benefits in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Prioritizing monoculture plantations for timber yields only"},{"id":"b","text":"Implementing forest restoration projects that enhance carbon sequestration and biodiversity"},{"id":"c","text":"Establishing protected areas without community involvement"},{"id":"d","text":"Promoting large-scale logging operations in primary forests"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00257', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In terms of multiple uses forestry, what method can enhance carbon sequestration, improve biodiversity, and provide economic benefits, particularly in degraded landscapes in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Slash-and-burn agriculture"},{"id":"b","text":"Intensive monoculture plantations"},{"id":"c","text":"Agroforestry with native species"},{"id":"d","text":"Open-pit mining expansion"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00258', 'forest-production', 'multiple-use-forestry', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of multiple uses forestry, which of the following approaches is most effective for ensuring the sustainable management of forest resources while balancing timber production and ecological preservation in the Philippines?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Implementing reduced impact logging coupled with the establishment of protected areas for biodiversity conservation."},{"id":"b","text":"Focusing solely on timber production with periodic assessments of forest health."},{"id":"c","text":"Allowing unrestricted access to forest resources to maximize economic benefits."},{"id":"d","text":"Designating entire forest regions exclusively for conservation purposes, excluding human activities."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00259', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the primary goal of the clearcutting silvicultural system?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To regenerate a stand as an uneven-aged cohort."},{"id":"b","text":"To regenerate a stand using advanced regeneration only."},{"id":"c","text":"To maintain a forest cover while selectively harvesting trees."},{"id":"d","text":"To remove the entire stand in one cutting and regenerate as an even-aged cohort."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00260', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'In which silvicultural method is artificial regeneration commonly used to establish seedlings after harvesting?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Selection system."},{"id":"b","text":"Clearcutting system."},{"id":"c","text":"Coppice system."},{"id":"d","text":"Shelterwood system."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00261', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which silvicultural system involves harvesting mature trees over several cuttings to create conditions favorable for natural regeneration under the partial canopy?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Clearcutting system."},{"id":"b","text":"Selection system."},{"id":"c","text":"Shelterwood system."},{"id":"d","text":"Coppice system."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00262', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What type of silvicultural system is commonly used to manage forests for continuous timber production by selectively harvesting individual trees or small groups?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Clearcutting system."},{"id":"b","text":"Shelterwood system."},{"id":"c","text":"Coppice system."},{"id":"d","text":"Selection system."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00263', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'In the context of silviculture, what does the term ''liberation cutting'' refer to?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Cutting to remove all trees in an area."},{"id":"b","text":"Cutting to establish an even-aged stand."},{"id":"c","text":"Cutting to harvest mature trees for timber."},{"id":"d","text":"Cutting to remove competing vegetation from around young trees."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00264', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which silvicultural system is primarily used to produce wood fuel or small diameter products from rapidly growing species?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Shelterwood system."},{"id":"b","text":"Clearcutting system."},{"id":"c","text":"Coppice system."},{"id":"d","text":"Selection system."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00265', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the main objective of the thinning operation in silviculture?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To reduce stand density and promote growth of remaining trees."},{"id":"b","text":"To increase biodiversity."},{"id":"c","text":"To remove diseased and defective trees only."},{"id":"d","text":"To convert an even-aged stand to an uneven-aged stand."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00266', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What does ''clearcutting with reserves'' involve in forestry management?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Leaving selected mature trees standing for wildlife habitat or aesthetic reasons."},{"id":"b","text":"Harvesting all trees and allowing natural seed dispersal."},{"id":"c","text":"Using clearcutting but planting seedlings immediately after."},{"id":"d","text":"Clearcutting followed by controlled burning."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00267', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'In which silvicultural method are stands typically regenerated from the sprouts of stumps or roots?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Shelterwood system."},{"id":"b","text":"Coppice system."},{"id":"c","text":"Clearcutting system."},{"id":"d","text":"Selection system."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00268', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What term describes the deliberate introduction of desired tree species into a forest stand to enhance its composition and structure?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Enrichment planting."},{"id":"b","text":"Thinning."},{"id":"c","text":"Clearcutting."},{"id":"d","text":"Liberation cutting."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00269', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which silvicultural method involves the removal of all trees in a specified area to establish a new uniform cohort?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Clearcutting"},{"id":"b","text":"Shelterwood"},{"id":"c","text":"Selection system"},{"id":"d","text":"Coppice"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00270', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'The selection system in silviculture is primarily characterized by which of the following practices?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Periodic removal of mature trees individually or in small groups"},{"id":"b","text":"Harvesting all trees at once"},{"id":"c","text":"Complete removal of overstory trees after regeneration is established"},{"id":"d","text":"Regeneration of trees from root suckers"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00271', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'In silviculture, what is the primary goal of applying a shelterwood system?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To remove all vegetation in a single operation"},{"id":"b","text":"To encourage regrowth from stumps and root sprouts"},{"id":"c","text":"To regenerate the forest using natural seeding under the protection of a partial canopy"},{"id":"d","text":"To selectively harvest only the oldest trees"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00272', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What is the primary purpose of a regeneration cutting in silvicultural systems?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To improve the aesthetic value of the forest"},{"id":"b","text":"To increase the diversity of wildlife habitat"},{"id":"c","text":"To reduce the risk of fire"},{"id":"d","text":"To create conditions suitable for establishing a new cohort of trees"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00273', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which silvicultural system is characterized by maintaining continuous forest cover and removing mature trees individually?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Clearcutting"},{"id":"b","text":"Coppice system"},{"id":"c","text":"Selection system"},{"id":"d","text":"Shelterwood"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00274', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'What does the term ''coppice'' refer to in silviculture?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"A system that relies on regeneration from seeds"},{"id":"b","text":"A method of regeneration from stump sprouts or root suckers"},{"id":"c","text":"A technique used to enhance wildlife habitat"},{"id":"d","text":"A type of thinning operation"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00275', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'In the context of silviculture, what is the main objective of a shelterwood cutting?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To clear the area of all vegetation"},{"id":"b","text":"To provide partial shade for regenerating seedlings"},{"id":"c","text":"To remove unhealthy trees to improve stand quality"},{"id":"d","text":"To encourage root sprouting for regeneration"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00276', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Easy', 'practice',
   'Which practice in silviculture involves cutting trees to stimulate seed production and natural regeneration under limited canopy cover?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Clearcutting"},{"id":"b","text":"Selection cutting"},{"id":"c","text":"Shelterwood system"},{"id":"d","text":"Coppice system"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00277', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which silvicultural method involves removing overstory trees to improve growth conditions for understory trees?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Liberation cutting"},{"id":"b","text":"Uniform shelterwood"},{"id":"c","text":"Coppicing"},{"id":"d","text":"Clearcutting"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00278', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In the selection system, what is the primary criterion for choosing which trees to harvest?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Age of the trees"},{"id":"b","text":"Species diversity"},{"id":"c","text":"Diameter at breast height (DBH)"},{"id":"d","text":"Proximity to road access"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00279', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which type of silvicultural system is best suited for maintaining continuous forest cover and biodiversity?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Clearcutting system"},{"id":"b","text":"Selection system"},{"id":"c","text":"Coppice system"},{"id":"d","text":"Uniform shelterwood system"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00280', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In a group selection system, which of the following benefits is most prominent?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Maintenance of an uneven-aged stand structure"},{"id":"b","text":"Creation of large open areas for new growth"},{"id":"c","text":"Increased vulnerability to pests"},{"id":"d","text":"Simplified harvesting operations"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00281', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'What is the main goal of applying a two-cut shelterwood system?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Enhance biodiversity by maintaining various age classes"},{"id":"b","text":"Increase the growth rate of existing understory trees"},{"id":"c","text":"Maximize short-term timber yield"},{"id":"d","text":"Promote even-aged stand management"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00282', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'What is a primary reason for using the seed tree method in silviculture?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To eliminate all existing vegetation and start anew"},{"id":"b","text":"To create a uniform age structure through planting"},{"id":"c","text":"To encourage natural regeneration by leaving a few mature trees"},{"id":"d","text":"To facilitate rapid canopy closure"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00283', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'How does the ''shelterwood with reserves'' system differ from a traditional shelterwood system?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It involves removing all trees at once."},{"id":"b","text":"It retains some mature trees for future harvests or ecological reasons."},{"id":"c","text":"It focuses on planting new trees rather than relying on natural regeneration."},{"id":"d","text":"It emphasizes the creation of large open areas for wildlife habitats."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00284', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which of the following is a characteristic of the coppice-with-standards system?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Regenerating from seeds only"},{"id":"b","text":"Leaving selected trees to grow larger while harvesting smaller coppice growth"},{"id":"c","text":"Harvesting all trees in one cutting"},{"id":"d","text":"Combining clearcutting and planting"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00285', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'What is the primary advantage of using strip clearcutting in silviculture?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Increases logging efficiency"},{"id":"b","text":"Creates uniform habitat conditions"},{"id":"c","text":"Minimizes soil erosion and nutrient loss"},{"id":"d","text":"Maximizes short-term timber yield"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00286', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In what situation is enrichment planting most beneficial in silvicultural practices?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"In degraded forests lacking desired species"},{"id":"b","text":"In dense primary forests with high biodiversity"},{"id":"c","text":"In newly established plantations"},{"id":"d","text":"In forests intended for non-timber products only"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00287', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which silvicultural system involves removing small groups of trees to create openings for regeneration, promoting a multi-aged forest structure?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Group selection system"},{"id":"b","text":"Clearcutting system"},{"id":"c","text":"Shelterwood system"},{"id":"d","text":"Coppice system"}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00288', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In the context of silvicultural systems, what is the primary goal of the seed tree method?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To remove all mature trees for immediate financial return"},{"id":"b","text":"To create a uniform stand age structure"},{"id":"c","text":"To reduce competition by removing understory vegetation"},{"id":"d","text":"To leave behind scattered trees for natural regeneration"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00289', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'What is the main purpose of applying a liberation cutting in a young plantation?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To stimulate seed production in mature trees"},{"id":"b","text":"To harvest all trees for maximum yield"},{"id":"c","text":"To promote understory vegetation growth"},{"id":"d","text":"To remove overstory trees and release suppressed trees below"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00290', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which of the following describes the main characteristic of the irregular shelterwood system?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Overstory trees are removed gradually to promote natural regeneration."},{"id":"b","text":"All trees are removed in one harvest and the area is replanted artificially."},{"id":"c","text":"Trees are harvested in small patches to maintain an uneven-aged structure."},{"id":"d","text":"Only the oldest trees are harvested to provide continuous coverage."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00291', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In the context of silviculture, what is the primary objective of a thinning operation in an uneven-aged stand?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To convert the stand into an even-aged structure"},{"id":"b","text":"To remove the youngest trees to increase light for the older ones"},{"id":"c","text":"To prepare the stand for immediate clearcutting"},{"id":"d","text":"To reduce stand density and improve tree growth and quality"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00292', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which silvicultural method specifically aims to enhance the structural complexity and biodiversity of a forest?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Clearcutting with reserves"},{"id":"b","text":"Continuous cover forestry"},{"id":"c","text":"Coppice system"},{"id":"d","text":"Monoculture plantation"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00293', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'What is the main benefit of implementing the strip clearcutting method in forest management?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"It creates a homogeneous age structure across the landscape"},{"id":"b","text":"It enhances windthrow resistance by leaving buffer strips"},{"id":"c","text":"It facilitates easy access for machinery and harvesting"},{"id":"d","text":"It promotes edge habitat for wildlife diversity"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00294', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In a silvicultural system, which practice involves retaining a portion of the forest canopy to partially shade the forest floor during regeneration?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Clearcutting"},{"id":"b","text":"Coppice system"},{"id":"c","text":"Shelterwood system"},{"id":"d","text":"Seed tree method"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00295', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'What is the primary goal of the clearcutting method when applied in a sustainable forestry context?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To maximize immediate timber yield without concern for regeneration"},{"id":"b","text":"To create conditions favorable for shade-tolerant species"},{"id":"c","text":"To establish a new even-aged stand for future harvesting"},{"id":"d","text":"To enhance biodiversity by removing all vegetation"}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00296', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which silvicultural method uses periodic cutting cycles to maintain continuous canopy cover while harvesting mature trees?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Clearcutting system"},{"id":"b","text":"Coppice system"},{"id":"c","text":"Shelterwood system"},{"id":"d","text":"Selection system"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00297', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'In the context of silvicultural methods, what is the primary purpose of applying a uniform shelterwood system?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To create multiple age classes within a stand for increased diversity."},{"id":"b","text":"To ensure even-aged regeneration by gradually removing the overstory."},{"id":"c","text":"To remove all trees in a single operation for immediate replanting."},{"id":"d","text":"To selectively thin the forest to promote growth of individual trees."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00298', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Medium', 'practice',
   'Which silvicultural system involves cutting small strips of trees to facilitate natural regeneration and minimize soil disturbance?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Seed tree method"},{"id":"b","text":"Clearcutting method"},{"id":"c","text":"Selection system"},{"id":"d","text":"Strip clearcutting method"}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00299', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In a silvicultural context, what is the main advantage of implementing the variable retention harvesting system?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Maximizing short-term timber yields."},{"id":"b","text":"Enhancing biodiversity by retaining key structural elements."},{"id":"c","text":"Facilitating rapid regeneration of even-aged stands."},{"id":"d","text":"Minimizing edge effects on adjacent stands."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00300', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which process in the selection silvicultural system ensures the recruitment of sufficient regeneration in the understory?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Regular application of prescribed burning to manage competition."},{"id":"b","text":"Periodic thinning of overstory trees to increase light penetration."},{"id":"c","text":"Selective fertilization of desirable species in the understory."},{"id":"d","text":"Harvesting dominant trees to reduce competition for resources."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00301', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'When applying a shelterwood system, which factor is critical to determine the timing of the final harvest cut?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"The growth rate of the regeneration cohort."},{"id":"b","text":"The maturity of the overstory trees."},{"id":"c","text":"Market demand for timber products."},{"id":"d","text":"The availability of logging equipment."}]'::jsonb, 'a'),
  ('fp-g00302', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of silviculture, how does the two-aged system differ fundamentally from the clearcutting system?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Clearcutting focuses on biodiversity conservation."},{"id":"b","text":"The two-aged system maintains elements of the previous stand structure."},{"id":"c","text":"The two-aged system involves complete canopy removal."},{"id":"d","text":"Clearcutting promotes uneven-aged stand development."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00303', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is a primary consideration in determining the appropriate residual basal area in a basal area retention system?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"The proximity to urban areas."},{"id":"b","text":"The desired light conditions for understorey regeneration."},{"id":"c","text":"The elevation of the site."},{"id":"d","text":"The historical land use patterns."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00304', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In a group selection system, how is the size of the group opening typically determined?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"According to the maximum allowable cut regulations."},{"id":"b","text":"In proportion to the average tree height in the stand."},{"id":"c","text":"By the number of trees that can be felled within a day."},{"id":"d","text":"Based on the target species'' light requirements for regeneration."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00305', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In uneven-aged management, what is the primary purpose of using diameter-limit cutting?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"To eliminate competition among trees of similar size."},{"id":"b","text":"To ensure the uniform growth rate of all trees in the stand."},{"id":"c","text":"To maximize timber yield by harvesting only the largest trees."},{"id":"d","text":"To selectively remove trees above a certain diameter to promote regeneration."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00306', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'What is a key characteristic of the irregular shelterwood system that differentiates it from a uniform shelterwood system?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"The use of mechanized logging exclusively."},{"id":"b","text":"The variability in the density and pattern of retained overstory trees."},{"id":"c","text":"The uniform age of the regeneration cohort."},{"id":"d","text":"The focus on non-timber forest products."}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00307', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In a coppice-with-standards system, what determines the rotation length for standard trees compared to coppice trees?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"The time required for coppice regrowth."},{"id":"b","text":"The prevalence of pest species in the area."},{"id":"c","text":"The market demand for coppice products."},{"id":"d","text":"The desired size and quality of standard timber."}]'::jsonb, 'd'),
  ('fp-g00308', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'Which of the following silvicultural systems involves the retention of certain trees for a longer period to benefit wildlife while allowing for timber extraction?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Irregular shelterwood system"},{"id":"b","text":"Shelterwood with reserves system"},{"id":"c","text":"Seed tree method"},{"id":"d","text":"Coppice system"}]'::jsonb, 'b'),
  ('fp-g00309', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'practice',
   'In the context of silvicultural systems, how does the group selection method differ from clearcutting in terms of forest structure and regeneration dynamics?',
   '[{"id":"a","text":"Group selection creates even-aged stands, whereas clearcutting results in uneven-aged forest structures."},{"id":"b","text":"Both methods result in a homogeneous stand structure but differ in harvesting intensity."},{"id":"c","text":"Group selection supports continuous canopy cover and diverse age classes, unlike clearcutting which leads to a single-aged cohort."},{"id":"d","text":"Clearcutting promotes natural regeneration, while group selection relies on artificial regeneration methods."}]'::jsonb, 'c'),
  ('fp-g00310', 'forest-production', 'silvicultural-methods-systems', 'Hard', 'practice',
